WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
Research Map · a quick tour
A fictional project: navigate research folders without moving the files.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.000
1 · Explore the graph
Click a folder node to expand its children.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
1 · Explore the graph
Baseline, faster-growth and comparison are peer analyses.

4
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
1 · Arrange your workspace
Drag a node to reposition it; use the graph controls to zoom or fit.

5
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
2 · Inspect an analysis
Right-click an analysis node and choose Inspect.

6
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
2 · Inspect an analysis
One record links the description, code, data, figures and metadata.

7
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
3 · Read code without leaving the graph
Open Python, JSON, Markdown and other text files in a read-only preview.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.000
4 · Find figures by folder
Inspect → Figures lists image files in their subfolder structure.

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
4 · Open the saved result
Inspect the figure directly. For multiple figures, use Previous/Next or ← →.

10
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
5 · Manage conversations by project
Manager highlights nodes with registered conversations. These are sample records.

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.000
5 · Give each conversation a home
Choose Selected node or Whole project, then give the conversation an objective.

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.000
6 · Find a conversation
Filter conversations by their objective. Titles stay attached to their nodes.

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:40.000
6 · Conversation actions
Right-click for a new linked session, recovery history, or recoverable deletion.

14
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
7 · Recover the context
Read saved checkpoints and history. This is a labelled sample checkpoint.

15
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.000
8 · Tidy up without losing the record
Delete hides a registered conversation. Undo restores it.

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
8 · Undo restores the conversation
The sample conversation is visible again, attached to the same analysis.

17
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Your research, connected
Try Orchard Study on GitHub. AI conversations use your own Codex CLI account.
